  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN217.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">pirivuṇarttiya tōḻikkut talaimaka ḷāṟṟāmai colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What SHE said about [her own] lack of strength to the confidante who informed [her] of the separation.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN217.1">
        <l>peytupulan tiṟanta poṅkal veṇmaḻai</l>
        <l>yeḵ<supplied>ku</supplied>ṟu pañciṟ ṟuytupaṭ ṭaṉṉa</l>
        <l>tuvalai tūval ka<supplied>ḻi</supplied>ya vakalvayi</l>
        <l>ṉiṭuka<supplied>ḻai</supplied>k karumpiṉ kaḷaikkāl vāṉpūk</l>
        <l>kōṭaip pūḷaiyiṉ vāṭaiyoṭu tuyalvara</l>
        <l>pā<supplied>ci</supplied>lai potuḷiya putaṟoṟum pakaṉṟai</l>
        <l>nīluṇ paccai niṟamaṟai<supplied>t ta</supplied>ṭaicciya </l>
        <l>tōleṟi pāṇ<supplied>ṭi</supplied>liṉ vāliya malarak</l>
        <l>kō<supplied>ḻilai</supplied> yavaraik koḻumukai yuṭaiya</l>
        <l>vūḻuṟu tōṉṟi yoṇpūt taḷaiviṭap</l>
        <l>pulantoṟuṅ kurukiṉa naralak kalleṉa</l>
        <l>vakaṉṟuṟai makaḷi raṇituṟantu naṭuṅka</l>
        <l>vacciram vantaṉ ṟamaintaṉ ṟituveṉa</l>
        <l>vepporuḷ peṟiṉum piriyaṉmi ṉōveṉac</l>
        <l>cep<supplied>pu</supplied>val vāḻiyō tuṇaiyiṭai yirkkē</l>
        <l>nalkāk kātalar nalaṉuṇṭu tuṟanta</l>
        <l>pāḻpaṭu mēṉi nōkki nōypora</l>
        <l>viṇariṟu puṭaiyu neñcamoṭu puṇarvuvēṭ</l>
        <l>ṭeyiṟu<supplied>tī</supplied>p piṟappat tiruki</l>
        <l>naṭuṅkutum piriyiṉyāṅ kaṭumpaṉi yuḻantē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="1">When the churning white clouds that opened over the fields have poured down</l>
        <l>[and], as the drizzling of drops passes that were falling like </l>
        <l corresp="2f">soft fibres of cotton put to the blade, in the vast area,</l>
        <l corresp="4">when the white flowers on the rugged stems of the sugarcane with steady stalks</l>
        <l corresp="5">come into swinging with the north wind as wool plants [do] in the west wind,</l>
        <l corresp="6">when on every bush that is dense with green leaves, the jalap</l>
        <l corresp="8">blooms in white [blossoms], like leather rounds under attack</l>
        <l corresp="7">on which [white] had been put, hiding the green colour that absorbed the blue(?),</l>
        <l corresp="9">while fat buds burst open on the field beans with fat leaves,</l>
        <l corresp="10">while the outer petals let go of the bright Malabar-lily flowers in [their] turn,</l>
        <l corresp="11">while flocks of herons trumpet in every field, noisily,</l>
        <l corresp="12">so that the women who stay in separation abandon [their] ornaments [and] shiver,</l>
        <l corresp="13">the cool season has come. “[This time] is suitable”, – since [HE] thought so,</l>
        <l corresp="14">“whatever kind of wealth may be obtained, please don’t part [from me]!”,</l>
        <l corresp="15">I say to you who is among [your] consorts , may you live.</l>
        <l corresp="16">While pain attacks [us] when looking at [our] ruined body</l>
        <l corresp="17">that is abandoned after [its] beauty had been consumed by an ungracious lover,</l>
        <l corresp="18">with a heart that breaks, broken [like a flower] cluster(?), wanting union,</l>
        <l corresp="19">gnashing [our] teeth so that sparks spring forth,</l>
        <l corresp="20">we will shiver if [HE] parts [from us], bearing the fierce dew.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
    </body>
